# Android WebView Pointer Tap Protocol

All active SilentPassUI touch controls must remain reliable in Android WebView,
including WebViews that report a finger as a `mouse` pointer.

## Required

- For tap-capable buttons, use `pointerup` through the shared
  `useReliableTapHandler` (not only `click`).
- Capture the pointer on `pointerdown`; accept `pointerup` only when movement
  stays within the shared tolerance, and suppress the browser's duplicate
  synthesized `click`.
- Mark priority controls with `data-touch-priority="1"` so AppShell's global
  touch guards do not call `preventDefault()` for their gesture.
- Apply `touchAction: manipulation` and the shared
  `RELIABLE_TAP_BUTTON_CLASS` to tap controls.
- Keep the global touch guards narrowly scoped to the active gesture. Every
  listener and temporary marker must be removed in cleanup; never add a
  permanent document-level tap side effect or a second parallel tap system.

## Audit boundary

This protocol applies to active `src/SilentPassUI` PWA/client UI only.
Abandoned native POS directories are not implementation targets.

